From dd9b69125418faad46e73fc03c6774ad022596ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:02:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_own_tempo_regression, v2_game_total_elasticity,
 v2_venue_mult and v2_rb_game_script

- v2_own_tempo_regression (2026-10-06): scale passing / receiving volume by 1 - kappa(G) x (team plays per game / league - 1),
  kappa 0.65 x max(0, 1 - G/10), capped at +-10%. Harness INCONCLUSIVE with no effect (START-ALL RMSE +0.002).
- v2_game_total_elasticity and v2_venue_mult: the implied-total and indoor/outdoor scalings unbundled from game_env; the shipped
  per-stat version (v2_game_total_elasticity_perstat) owns the implied-total channel. Never backtested standalone.
- v2_rb_game_script (2026-11-01, backlog L5): the rushing-only margin scaling plus RB receiving yards scaled down with the margin.
  The rushing part shipped as v2_rb_game_script_rush; the receiving term made RB receiving yards worse (held out 5 of 5 seasons,
  harness 3 of 4).
Removes the tempo section (TEMPO_* and own_tempo_multiplier), the two standalone environment switches (game_env still gates the legacy
bundle), the all-stats RB_GAME_SCRIPT table, a sweep script and the tempo tests. Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
